# Comma-separated logins permitted to use the application (exactly five, admin included).
AIC_ALLOWED_USERS=owner@example.com,teammate1@example.com,teammate2@example.com,teammate3@example.com,teammate4@example.com
AIC_ADMIN_USER=owner@example.com

# No Basic Auth and no HAProxy-side identity var needed: identity comes from `tailscale serve`'s
# Tailscale-User-Login header (see haproxy.cfg), which is only trusted from loopback/the docker
# bridge. Each entry above must match that teammate's real Tailscale account login once they are
# invited onto the tailnet, or they get 403.
#
# Split development only: a teammate's app forwards compute to the owner's `/core/*` endpoints
# through that same tailnet URL. Leave unset on the owner's host (production) so everything runs
# locally. `AIC_CORE_USER` is only needed when the owner runs uvicorn without HAProxy, which
# cannot set X-AIC-User itself. See docs/split-development.md.
# AIC_CORE_URL=https://tanp21-desktop.taild28bdb.ts.net
# AIC_CORE_USER=teammate1@example.com

# Venue deployment: compute on a rented instance, media on the laptop in the exam room. The
# laptop sets AIC_ROLE=media so it answers the SPA and /thumb /frame /video /clip from its own
# disk and forwards every other route to the instance, and AIC_CORE_URL to reach it. The
# instance sets AIC_MEDIA_HOST_LOGIN to the laptop's own tailnet login, which is the only
# identity whose X-AIC-Delegated-User it will believe -- without it the whole team shares one
# coordinator slot and one agent run. See docs/venue-deployment.md.
# AIC_ROLE=media                        # laptop only; leave unset on the instance
# AIC_MEDIA_HOST_LOGIN=teammate1@example.com   # instance only; the laptop's tailnet login

# -- "Check by AI" (Search tab) and the retrieval agent's judge ---------------------------------
# One OpenRouter key for the whole team. The Search tab's check button is hidden when this is
# unset (`GET /session` reports only whether it is there, never the key). A check costs well
# under a cent, so nobody pastes anything -- unlike the Retrieval agent tab's per-run DeepSeek
# and Gemini keys, which are one teammate's personal quota.
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=qwen/qwen3.7-flash   # text + image in, structured output, 1M context
# AIC_CHECK_WINDOW_SECONDS=300          # +-5 minutes around the frame, the UI default
# AIC_CHECK_TTL_SECONDS=3600            # how long a check and a query's checklist stay cached
#
# Setting this also lets the retrieval agent judge with OpenRouter instead of Gemini, which is
# what to do when the Gemini quota is gone. Web lookups stay on Gemini (Google Search grounding)
# and are simply skipped without a Gemini key.
# AIC_AGENT_VISION=openrouter
